r:"}},{"type":"text","value":" that silently\nnever fires. An application's build checks the relations whose module it\ncompiled, so a shared component may read an ancestor that only some\napplications render; "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> check","source":"kirana-style check"}},{"type":"text","value":" checks every relation in the project."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"relation-placement","source":"relation-placement"}}]},{"type":"text","value":": the anchor cannot be proven to be in the right\nposition: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">after</span>()","source":"after()"}},{"type":"text","value":" used where the anchor is not an earlier sibling, for\nexample."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A relation that is declared and never read is reported too ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"relation-unused","source":"relation-unused"}},{"type":"text","value":"),\nso dead relations do not accumulate. And because a relation is identified by its\npackage and name, two modules of one package that both write "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">relation</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;card&quot;</span>)","source":"relation(\"card\")"}},{"type":"text","value":"\nwould share one marker without meaning to: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"relation-name-collision","source":"relation-name-collision"}},{"type":"text","value":" names both\nfiles. Export the relation from one module and import it where it is read."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"anchors-are-placed-not-guessed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anchors are placed, not guessed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The anchor must sit on the element whose state you are reading. That sounds\nobvious, and it is the most common mistake when porting: the state lives on the\nroot, the anchor gets attached to an inner wrapper, and the read never matches."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"// The attribute and the anchor belong on the same element.\n<div data-state={open ? \"open\" : \"closed\"} sx={[menu.anchor, styles.root]}>","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// The attribute and the anchor belong on the same element.</span>\n&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">div</span> data-<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">state</span>={open ? <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;open&quot;</span> : <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;closed&quot;</span>} <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={[menu.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">anchor</span>, styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">root</span>]}&gt;"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"has-is-not-a-relation","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":":has()"},{"type":"text","value":" is not a relation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Styling a parent by its children is a plain condition, because the selector does\nit on its own:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({\n  paddingBlockEnd: { \":has([data-slot='footer'])\": \"0.5rem\" },\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">paddingBlockEnd</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;:has([data-slot=&#39;footer&#39;])&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0.5rem&quot;</span> },\n})"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Relations exist for the other direction (a descendant or sibling reading state\nthat lives elsewhere), where CSS needs the two ends to agree on a class."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"precedence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Precedence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A relation read is its own condition class, ranked below attributes and\npseudo-classes on the element itself, and above at-rules\n("},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/precedence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ladder"}]},{"type":"text","value":", step 3). So an element's own "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":":hover","source":":hover"}},{"type":"text","value":" beats a\nvalue that depends on an ancestor's "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":":hover","source":":hover"}},{"type":"text","value":", which is what an author usually\nmeans."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"relations","text":"Relations","level":1},{"id":"the-three-reads","text":"The three reads","level":2},{"id":"why-declare-it-at-all","text":"Why declare it at all","level":2},{"id":"anchors-are-placed-not-guessed","text":"Anchors are placed, not guessed","level":2},{"id":"has-is-not-a-relation","text":":has() is not a relation","level":2},{"id":"precedence","text":"Precedence","level":2}]}
